<title>DUBAI: TABLE-Ominvest H1 attrib sharply higher.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Ominvest H1 attrib sharply higher.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>			    (million Omani rials)</p>
<p> Net profit			     6.611	vs	3.273</p>
<p>Profit attributable to</p>
<p>    Ominvest shareholders	   4.792	vs	1.927</p>
<p>Profit attributable to</p>
<p>    minority interests		1.819	vs	1.346</p>
<p> Share of associates' profit	0.255	vs	0.266</p>
<p> Interest income			8.324	vs	6.952</p>
<p> Investment income		    4.396	vs	1.498</p>
<p> Forex, commission, other income  1.640	vs	1.422</p>
<p> Shareholders funds		  27.722	vs     22.930</p>
<p> Total assets			 254.582	vs    221.921</p>
<p>Full name: Oman International Development and Investment Co SAOG.</p>
<p>Note - The figures are unaudited. The company said first half net profit was the firm's highest, surpassing previous record profit of 3.621 million rials for the whole of 1996.</p>
<p>It said the increase was due to the significant gain realised on the sale of its 20 percent stake in Gibcorp Oman, exceptional returns on its securities portfolio and good results recorded by the firm's subsidiaries and associates.</p>
<p>-- Dubai newsroom +9714 6071 222</p>
</text>
